Well, I'd just like to respond to that for a moment, if you don't mind...

I've played Nethack since back in the days when it was Hack 1.03...
I've always loved the game, and I've always used "save/restore strategy"...
I don't feel that I'm competing against anyone else, and I'm only
playing at all because I enjoy exploring, wandering around and seeing
what I find, etc etc etc... 
 
I find that I become VERY attached to one character when I'm playing
him, and really am not willing to spend 100 hours or so running a
really neat char, then have him die (permanently) thru some random
event... I rather resent having people suggest that I'm somehow 
"cheating" when I ressurect a favoured character - who can I possibly
cheat???   I'm getting what I want out of the game (it IS a game,
after all), and what I do on my PC has NO effect on any other player
other than myself... 
 
Nethack seems to have been carefully designed to thrill and excite
those who enjoy this style of game... after five years of almost
continuous play, it STILL EXCITES ME!!!  It excites you too, right???
     
       so who am I cheating???

